  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We have a single data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc). We know nothing about whether the image modality contributes useful signal, which is the central premise of a multimodal study. 2) What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides a clean single-modality baseline for the image branch, directly answering whether spatial/morphological features are informative for this task. 3) Why best next: This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-leverage question. If image features are uninformative, the entire multimodal block (configs 016–051) is deprioritized and we should invest in RNA encoder or profile-setting improvements. If they are informative, multimodal fusion becomes a promising exploitation direction. Using resnet50 (the same encoder in configs 016–021) and keeping singleprofile ensures a controlled comparison: later, config_016 vs config_010 vs config_001 will cleanly isolate the additive/fusion contribution of combining modalities. Changing only the modality (keeping profile setting identical) avoids confounding multiple design choices at once."
}

